1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:06,310
We have a project around campus dogs, where community outreach is part of it.

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:13,470
And we wanted to know about your personal experience and what you think about dogs in the area?

3
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:25,810
like if you are in a road con, late nights come there

4
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:27,370
then you face some issues

5
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:30,090
I don't have any experience

6
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:38,590
You can't tell which dog is friendly or which one is a little bit senpy

7
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:41,750
So when I meet any of those dogs

8
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,610
I pet them a little

9
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:47,510
I was walking from the garden near the mat

10
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:55,250
I was just about to pet them and one of my dogs bit me.

11
00:00:56,430 --> 00:01:01,490
Which is very rare, it doesn't happen often but once he bit me,

12
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:05,670
I got scared and I was waiting for him.

13
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:09,650
Many of my friends get scared of their dogs in general.

14
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:11,230
They can't go anywhere.

15
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:15,310
Recently we were hosting a birthday party for my friend

16
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:50,770
They get scared easily.

17
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:53,290
One of them bit my friend.

18
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:56,950
So, we should keep an eye on them.

19
00:01:57,010 --> 00:02:00,690
We should not let aggressive dogs bite them.

20
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:04,150
So, when you have bitten someone,

21
00:02:05,030 --> 00:02:06,350
your opinion has changed?

22
00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:07,730
Do you now pet dogs?

23
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:11,670
No, I don't pet them.

24
00:02:11,830 --> 00:02:14,030
But they are not afraid of me.

25
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:16,650
I don't see a dog running away from fear.

26
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:27,930
If you are bitten by a dog, you will go back to the owner.

27
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:29,670
It can happen.

28
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:32,530
What do you think after seeing the actions of the admin?

29
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:36,870
Is the admin pro or anti-dog?

30
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:41,390
Our administration

31
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:46,330
Do you think some actions are being taken actively?

32
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:48,490
No, no action is being taken.

33
00:02:49,110 --> 00:02:49,770
And what should be taken?

34
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:53,130
What do you think is the middle ground in the case of dogs?

35
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:09,430
If there is any problem with the administration, we will ask them.

36
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,550
We can tell them.

37
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:13,690
So we should remove all the existing blocks from here.

38
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:16,210
And they should be kept out of the hostel too.

39
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:19,330
Hostels have a lot of hygiene issues.

40
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:24,590
They go to their beds and make the rooms dirty.

41
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:27,970
So they should be kept away from the hostel.

42
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:33,390
People forget that animals are there.

43
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:40,130
But after that, when they are destroying things, you guys come and clean it.

44
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:42,350
And no one cleans it.

45
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:44,110
If you have seen the test, then don't give it to them.

46
00:03:44,270 --> 00:03:44,950
It creates hygiene issues.

47
00:03:45,410 --> 00:03:47,670
Due to this, diseases can be outbreak of many diseases.

48
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:48,630
Mosquitoes can also get outbreak.

49
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:51,490
I think it's better to start from hostel.

50
00:03:52,670 --> 00:03:58,210
If you want to take care of so much, there are multiple such outside things on campus

51
00:03:58,210 --> 00:03:59,830
where you can meet.

52
00:04:00,670 --> 00:04:02,290
So we will not find better things there.

53
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:05,010
How is the medical response here?

54
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:06,250
Like you just got bitten by a dog.

55
00:04:06,590 --> 00:04:09,670
How's the IT staff here when it comes to dog bites?

56
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:12,650
It's very average.

57
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:15,850
It's not that good but it's not bad.

58
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:19,830
So, they do take care of you if there are no better options?

59
00:04:19,970 --> 00:04:20,470
Yes.

